      <div class="signal-shell">
        <SignalSubjectMenu current="science" class="evidence-topics" />
        <div class="evidence-hero-grid">
          <div>
            <p class="evidence-kicker">Brief 006 · Real-time AI</p>
            <h1>Can AI close the loop<br><em>before the world moves?</em></h1>
            <p class="evidence-deck">Evaluate a bounded task, not a model, profession, or industry. Speed matters only when sensing, interpretation, prediction, decision, action, and observation finish inside the task’s changing environment.</p>
            <div class="evidence-meta"><span>Curated evidence reviewed <strong id="realtime-review-date">2026-09-01</strong></span><span>Six bounded cases</span><a href="#sources">Inspect source ledger</a></div>
          </div>
          <aside class="evidence-verdict evidence-bearing" data-source-id="ca-dmv-permits fda-idx-dr jhm-retina amazon-robin nist-ai-rmf" aria-label="Current verdict">
            <span>Current read · conditional</span>
            <strong>Some bounded loops close. Few justify broad autonomy claims.</strong>
            <p>Timing success and benchmark accuracy do not establish field reliability, authority, scale, safety, or position removal.</p>
            <p class="proximate-citation" data-citation-source-id="ca-dmv-permits fda-idx-dr jhm-retina amazon-robin">Evidence basis: bounded operation documented by <a href="https://www.dmv.ca.gov/portal/vehicle-industry-services/autonomous-vehicles/autonomous-vehicle-testing-permit-holders/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">California DMV</a> · <a href="https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/cdrh_docs/reviews/DEN180001.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">FDA</a> · <a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41746-024-01197-3" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Johns Hopkins field deployment</a> · <a href="https://www.amazon.science/publications/pick-planning-strategies-for-large-scale-package-manipulation" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Amazon production evidence</a>.</p>
            <p class="proximate-citation" data-citation-source-id="nist-ai-rmf">Evidence basis: methodology and risk caution from <a href="https://www.nist.gov/publications/artificial-intelligence-risk-management-framework-ai-rmf-10" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">NIST AI RMF 1.0 ↗</a> · <a href="#source-nist-ai-rmf">scope &amp; caveats ↓</a></p>
          </aside>
        </div>

