          <aside id="case-detail" class="case-detail" aria-live="polite" aria-labelledby="case-detail-title">
            <header><p class="evidence-label">Selected task boundary</p><h3 id="case-detail-title">Geofenced autonomous driving</h3><span id="case-detail-timing">Operational real time</span></header>
            <dl>
              <div><dt>Boundary</dt><dd id="case-detail-boundary">Dynamic driving task inside a permit-defined operational design domain; not unrestricted driving.</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Deadline</dt><dd id="case-detail-deadline">Vehicle-control cycle before road state invalidates the action; exact deadline is system-specific.</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Human fallback</dt><dd id="case-detail-fallback">Remote assistance, minimal-risk stop, passenger or fleet support, and emergency services; exact design is operator-specific.</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Failure boundary</dt><dd id="case-detail-failure">Outside approved geography, weather, speed, road type, sensor visibility, or system capability; rare interactions and incident recovery.</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Scope / period / intended use</dt><dd id="case-detail-scope">California public roads; permitted manufacturers and vehicles; California permit status reviewed through August 2026; federal crash-reporting framework amended through 2025. Intended use: Navigate, control speed, and respond to road users within approved location, weather, speed, and operating constraints.</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Interpretation / caveat</dt><dd id="case-detail-read">Public-road operation demonstrates a bounded closed loop and regulatory authorization in named domains. Caveat: Permits are not proof of comparative safety. Raw report counts are not incident counts or comparative safety rates; reports can be duplicated and lack exposure denominators.</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <p id="case-detail-sources" class="case-detail__sources"><a href="https://www.dmv.ca.gov/portal/vehicle-industry-services/autonomous-vehicles/autonomous-vehicle-testing-permit-holders/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">California Department of Motor Vehicles ↗</a> <a href="https://www.nhtsa.gov/laws-regulations/standing-general-order-crash-reporting" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">US National Highway Traffic Safety Administration ↗</a></p>
          </aside>

